<article class="env-lemma" id="0BNZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BNZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0BNZ">15.92.13</span>.</a> Let $(R \to R', f)$ be a glueing pair. Then $\text{Tor}^ R_1(R', f^ n R) = 0$ for each $n > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      From the exact sequence $0 \to R[f^ n] \to R \to f^ n R \to 0$ we see that it suffices to check that $R[f^ n] \otimes _ R R' \to R'$ is injective. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0BNK" data-tag="0BNK">15.90.9</a> we have $R[f^ n] \otimes _ R R' = R[f^ n]$ and by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BNR" data-tag="0BNR">15.92.6</a> we see that $R[f^ n] \to R'$ is injective as $(R \to R', f)$ is a glueing pair. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>